ngth that  means it can skip up floors if a window  is open on a floor above as many would  have been on a hot London night the  flame can spread back into the building  on another floor what it shows and what  it says is basically that there are  regulations in place in this country  that need to be followed in order to  avoid the risks and if they're not  followed if  that the safeguards associated with  cladding are not properly put in place  then yes there is a risk that cladding  can contribute to a fire 18 months ago  the report said that small-scale tests  for cladding were not an effective way  of evaluating a live fire situation the  husk of Grenfell tower stands as  testament to that  Tom Cheshire Sky News
 

